cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A small language model as an offline store kiosk assistant"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Choudhary"
    given-names: "Anany Dev"
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur"
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An offline retail kiosk assistant built on small language models (2 and 4 billion parameters) running with
  llama.cpp on a laptop processor and integrated graphics, with hybrid retrieval, a tool-running harness,
  LoRA adapters, a kiosk app, and a pre-registered evaluation on fictional data across five objectives.
keywords:
  - small language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - tool calling
  - on-device inference
  - llama.cpp
  - retail kiosk
